<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  fleet-broker-tunnel — put keyvault's forgejo-broker socket on THIS host.

  infra ADR-0003 §2. The watcher no longer holds the owner's Forgejo admin PAT;
  it asks the broker on vaulthost for the protection verdict. The broker listens on a
  unix socket (never a TCP port — a LAN port would have to authenticate callers
  with something they HOLD, which is the copyable-bearer defect ADR-0002 exists
  to remove, reintroduced in front of the credential ADR-0003 exists to hide).
  So the socket is forwarded here instead.

  WHY A PERSISTENT FORWARD RATHER THAN ssh-PER-CALL. The retired helper ssh'd to
  vaulthost ONCE per cycle for a token that was then reused for every repo. Asking the
  broker is per-REPO, so the naive port of it would ssh ~20 times a cycle — the
  exact pattern that filled opshost with ~90k TIME_WAIT sockets and broke TCP on
  2026-08-2x. One long-lived connection, multiplexed by the forward.

  WHAT REPLACES THIS. Nothing in eunomia knows this is ssh: fleet-watch connects
  to a LOCAL socket path (FLEET_BROKER_SOCKET) and holds no credential. When
  SPIRE reaches opshost, a Ghostunnel sidecar presents an SVID at the same path and
  this job goes away. That is the ADR-0002 shape — the app holds nothing, a
  co-located sidecar terminates — with ssh standing in for the sidecar meanwhile.

  Install (opshost only — the host fleet-watch runs on):
    mkdir -p ~/run ~/dev/.fleet
    cp launchd/org.eunomia.fleet-broker-tunnel.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-broker-tunnel.plist
  Reload after editing (a frozen daemon needs bootout+bootstrap, not kickstart):
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/org.eunomia.fleet-broker-tunnel
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-broker-tunnel.plist
  Verify the postcondition, not the exit code — that the socket ANSWERS.
  Use the broker's own query script, which defaults to this path:
    ~/bao/broker/forgejo-broker-query.sh operator/keyvault
  (or curl with its unix-socket option against ~/run/forgejo-broker.sock;
  written out rather than shown because a double dash cannot appear inside
  an XML comment. launchd tolerates one; plistlib and expat do not.)

  If this job is down the watcher pages ONCE and scans nothing. It does not
  refuse every repo; see broker_verdict() and ADR-0003 §6.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>org.eunomia.fleet-broker-tunnel</string>

  <!-- -N: no remote command, forwarding only. The LOCAL socket is removed first
       because ssh refuses to bind an existing path, and an unclean stop leaves
       one behind — without the rm the job crash-loops on "Address already in
       use" and the watcher reads the fleet as blind.
       ExitOnForwardFailure makes ssh exit non-zero if it cannot ESTABLISH the
       forward, which for -L means the local bind. Be exact about what that does
       NOT cover: a -L unix forward connects to the REMOTE socket lazily, per
       connection, so with the broker down on vaulthost ssh stays up and accepts then
       closes each local connection. That is a live tunnel answering nothing,
       and this option does not prevent it. It is handled a layer up instead —
       an accept-then-close renders as status 0 in _broker_get, which is
       UNDETERMINED, and the message names both the tunnel and the broker. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>rm -f "$HOME/run/forgejo-broker.sock"; exec /usr/bin/ssh -N -T -o BatchMode=yes -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -L "$HOME/run/forgejo-broker.sock:/Users/operator/bao/run/forgejo-broker.sock" vaulthost</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- KeepAlive unconditionally, including on a clean exit: ssh exiting 0 after
       the far side closes is still an outage of the forward. ThrottleInterval
       stops a vaulthost reboot turning into a reconnect storm. -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>15</integer>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <!-- Absolute on purpose, and inconsistent with the $HOME in
       ProgramArguments for a reason: launchd does NOT expand $HOME in a
       path key, only the shell above expands it in the command. A
       missing StandardOutPath directory silently prevents the job from
       starting, so this is the one place the literal home has to appear.
       Replace it if this is ever installed under another account. -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/broker-tunnel.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/broker-tunnel.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
